{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-jet-prolongation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:jet-prolongation","kind":"proposition","title":"Jet Prolongation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-observable-universe"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-jet-prolongation"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-jet-prolongation-su2","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-prolongation-categorical","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-brane-tower-levels"],"tags":["jet-bundle","frobenius-hopf","prolongation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.JetProlongation","text":"jet-prolongation.md","leanSource":"jet-prolongation.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:jet-prolongation\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Jet Prolongation</em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe over a ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> (<a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\">quantum observable universe</a>). We define the <em>jet object</em>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  J^1(A) := A \\otimes \\Omega^1(A),</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^1(A) = \\ker(m \\colon A \\otimes A \\to A)</code> is the bimodule of Kähler differentials. The space <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^1(A)</code> inherits a canonical Frobenius–Hopf structure directly from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>. The quadruple <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, J^1(A), \\tau', q)</code>—with the induced fibre functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau' = \\tau \\circ (\\text{--} \\otimes \\Omega^1)</code>—forms a quantum observable universe over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>.</p>\n"}
